sieve-filter-v2
; A phrase that comes home: the last event is a note on the tonic (any octave), and the note before it is a
; step away, one or two semitones above or below (with `approach` half, one semitone only: the leading note
; below, or the note above it). A note repeated keeps how it was reached, so D C C ends by a step too. Rests
; break the approach: a rest just before the last note does not count as a step. The state is the last event's
; pitch (0: a rest, or nothing yet) and whether it was reached by a step.
id        melody-cadence
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  The melody ends on the tonic, reached by a step from the note before.
param     tonic     choice  C C,C#,D,D#,E,F,F#,G,G#,A,A#,B the note to end on
param     approach  choice  step step,half a step of one or two semitones, or of one only

states    {2 * (PITCHES + 1)}
start     0
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  if {(LOW + p - 1) % 12 == tonic}
    accept  {2 * p + 1}
  fi
done
for f 0 1
  for p 0 {PITCHES}
    for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
      t {2 * p + f} @{d} 0
      for q 1 {PITCHES}
        if {p >= 1 && abs(q - p) >= 1 && abs(q - p) <= 2 - approach}
          t {2 * p + f} @{q * DURATIONS + d} {2 * q + 1}
        else
          if {q == p}
            t {2 * p + f} @{q * DURATIONS + d} {2 * q + f}
          else
            t {2 * p + f} @{q * DURATIONS + d} {2 * q}
          fi
        fi
      done
    done
  done
done
end
